1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,090
mbLP Wave 2 · deposit BTC, earn MEZO as BTC/MUSD liquidity · v6 live on Mezo testnet

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:08,800
The Vault page defaults to v6: one deposit opens a MUSD trove, borrows, adds liquidity and stakes it in Mezo's live gauge

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,370
Live from the chain: trove collateral ratio 288% (target 300%), idle 0.002000 BTC / 0 MUSD

4
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:20,950
Try to break it: 12 live attacks on the deployed vault from a stranger's address. 11 refused, 1 harmless, 0 got through

5
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:28,520
Every row shows the contract's own revert reason: OnlySelf, DepositCapReached, ERC20InsufficientBalance, NotAuthorized from Mezo's gauge

6
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:36,080
Economic attacks, measured in tests: sandwiching a keeper step, deposit or withdrawal costs the attacker at 2%, 6% and 10% bands

7
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:41,160
Wave 2: I attacked the vault against MUSD's real rules. Every fix has a test that failed before it

8
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:46,230
MUSD's borrowing cap: the vault now refinances its trove, so a 13x deposit deploys in full

9
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:51,290
Recovery Mode: exits now stay open and pay each holder their NAV share

10
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:57,370
Deployment sandwich: steps are a tenth of the pool, so sandwiching it loses money

11
00:00:57,370 --> 00:01:03,440
A fall with the pool left behind: rebalance may cut debt, and attacking it earns nothing

12
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:09,500
v6: new debt is capped by the collateral ratio it leaves, so a deployment no longer reverts

13
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:17,080
Community page: 1 outside depositor so far, read from chain with the transaction (team wallets excluded)

14
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:22,660
v6 source verified on the Mezo explorer · 96 tests including a 65,536-action invariant suite, 8 fork tests on testnet and mainnet

15
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:26,210
mblp.surge.sh · github.com/GuTS805/Akindo · testnet only, unaudited
